{"step_index":838,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T11:22:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-26T11:22:21Z\nCompleted At: 2026-10-26T11:22:21Z\nShowing lines 1-89 of 89\n1: # Network Operations\n2: \n3: This is the authoritative documentation for the current network state.\n4: \n5: ## Settled Design (2026-10-19)\n6: **Architecture:** One two-way WARP tunnel (`wgcf-ingress`) from the decoy to the host.\n7: - **Tunnel Characteristics:**\n8:   - Decoy terminates WireGuard (`wg-opdbus`, 10.0.0.1).\n9:   - Decoy seals peer identity (OIA1).\n10:   - fwmark selects `wgcf-ingress` for egress.\n11:   - a simple plain TCP port (8090) is the target.\n12: - **Addressing:**\n13:   - Public host addressing: `pub0`.\n14:   - Internal fabric: `ovsbr0` retains OpenFlow `10.200.0.1`.\n15: - **Decoy Routing:**\n16:   - Administrative SSH (TCP 22/2222) is DNAT'd from `10.0.0.1` to `188.68.58.237:22` via table `ip wgcf_admin_ssh`.\n17: - **SOP:** No inner tunnels (GRE, SSH TUN, MASQUE, Xray) are required or active.\n18: \n19: ## Recovery evidence and deployment state (2026-10-20)\n20: - **Interfaces:** `ovsbr0` is UP and holds `10.0.0.2/32` (as an alias). `pub0` is the public uplink.\n21: - **Routing:** Local routing for `10.0.0.0/24` looks up table `28061`.\n22: - **Verified recovery:** `10.0.0.2:8090` listens and CA-verified HTTPS `/mcp` returns `401` for an unauthenticated request. Private listeners `127.0.0.1:1883`, `127.0.0.1:8085`, and `127.0.0.1:9000` are present.\n23: - **Verified MQTT path:** CA-verified `/mqtt` WebSocket upgrade through `10.0.0.2:8090` returns `101` with MQTT subprotocol. The private ExHook `https://127.0.0.1:9000/` responds `200` using the existing verified CA and client certificate.\n24: - **Release state:** Slot A has complete readiness; bridge and EMQX pass their real health checks using approved, backed-up maintenance overrides under `/var/lib/opdbus-release/maintenance-8090-20261020`. Corrected GNU bridge and opblob were built and a corrected golden filesystem prepared.\n25: - **Canonical deployment blocker (superseded 2026-10-20 ~22:44Z):** Reusing inactive root 450 had failed the exact-generation c\n<truncated 15519 bytes>\nn started only after deployment and remains pending.\n77: \n78: ## Current network — owner correction (2026-10-20)\n79: \n80: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.  \n81: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.  \n82: ONLY SERVICE INGRESS ENDPOINT: 10.0.0.2:8090. EMQX IS NOT ON 10.0.0.3.\n83: \n84: - Door, EMQX and Qdrant are reached through that one service ingress endpoint.\n85: - EMQX private backends remain on `127.0.0.1`: MQTT `1883`, management API `18083`, wake WSS `8085`. The existing bridge relays `wss://10.0.0.2:8090/mqtt` to the private WSS backend. Port `8084` remains owned by threetched.\n86: - The bridge's private ExHook backend is `https://127.0.0.1:9000`; retain TLS peer verification and the existing client certificate. MQTT CONNECT authentication and owner-topic authorization remain enforced.\n87: - `ovsbr0` retains OpenFlow `10.200.0.1`. No `10.0.0.3` broker alias is required or authorized by this correction.\n88: - Latest native deployment readiness, `2026-10-23T00:15:07Z`: `complete b release-67847196-f07a-4538-a4ba-4d2ec2a59938`, active root460/source459, previous A/root458/source457, no transaction in progress. Canonical activation completed with its built-in service readiness gates; bridge PID5494 executable SHA256 `c8937c7dee5f6b2f8e87ec060f1adf07ef9d693016448c0fe6179a6b8a25580b` matches the retained build. Live and persisted catalog manifests both hash to `0badd9cd84b7868f25ff04c1567996edd39ea214d195c94074d5c908cd2ab988`; the existing catalog was retained, not resealed. No reboot. Registered human credential admission, provider enumeration and the connected surface succeed in the router-backed deployed-UI check above; the user's own browser reconnect and actual model inference remain unverified.\n89: - This document is the sole location for network operational notes. Append future changes here, keeping the current network as the final section; do not duplicate network history, topology, status or notices in `SIGNALS.md` or `HANDOFF.md`.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
